  "summary": "Import-time remote code fetch-and-execute over plain HTTP",
  "details": "On require of the package's main entry (src/inout.js), code performs an unconditional http.get to http://tailwindlan.online, writes the response body to a sibling file, and immediately require()s that file, executing arbitrary attacker-controlled JavaScript in the consuming Node process with full privileges. The transport is plain HTTP with no integrity check, so both the origin host and any on-path attacker can deliver code. The package's name, README, and repository field impersonate the first-party @tailwindcss/aspect-ratio plugin published by tailwindlabs, while the actual shipped code contains only the remote loader.",
